    "result_text": "Full suite green \u2014 277 tests, 0 failures. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe specification required telephone numbers to be stored as digits-only, returned in the `telephone` field, with normalization applied *before* the uniqueness check so `(613) 555-0100` and `6135550100` are treated as the same number.\n\nTwo changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Relaxed the `telephone` validation pattern from `^[0-9]*$` to `^[0-9 ()-]*$`. This was necessary because `OwnerFieldsDto` is bean-validated with `@Valid` at request binding; the old pattern would have rejected a formatted number with a 400 before any normalization could run.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 `setTelephone(...)` now normalizes by stripping whitespace, dashes, and parentheses (`replaceAll(\"[\\\\s()-]\", \"\")`) before storing. Making this a domain invariant means:\n   - The MapStruct mapper (which calls `setTelephone`) stores the canonical digits-only value, so the entity's `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{10}$\")` validates the normalized 10-digit value and it round-trips back in the `telephone` field.\n   - The existing uniqueness checks (`existsOwnerWithTelephone` and `existsIdenticalOwner`) compare the already-normalized candidate value against already-normalized stored values, so formatting differences collapse to the same number \u2014 satisfying the \"before the uniqueness check\" requirement without touching the controller/service logic.\n\nBoth new `Cp11Tests` pass (`coreStoresDigitsOnly`, `functionalityNormalisedDuplicateRejected`), and all 277 tests remain green.",
